findings.claim:
Each day, fetch DRAO F10.7 (three readings a day), RSTN noon fluxes (410-4995 MHz from four stations) and the IPS Learmonth interpolated quiet-Sun values from SWPC's JSON and the IPS list. Then:
- compare at the same hour;
- use observed, not adjusted, flux (±3.4 % annual Earth-Sun distance);
- drop times listed as bursts (RBR) in SWPC events;
- treat the single-polarisation reading as I/2.
Track the ratio of array16's value to the reference over days; its scatter measures instrument stability. Expect about ±10 % against RSTN and about 1-2 % against DRAO when observing at 2695 MHz; the IPS ratio of 2790 to 2695 MHz at minimum is +3 %. An array16 sweep could cover 0.40-0.87 GHz in about 0.05-0.17 s (estimate).
